{"schema": 2, "id": "ruler-_Wu_Zhou", "title": "Wu Zhou", "label": "Wu Zhou", "description": "Chinese imperial dynasty (690–705)", "extract": "Zhou, known in historiography as the Wu Zhou, was a short-lived Chinese imperial dynasty that existed between 690 and 705. The dynasty consisted of the reign of one female emperor, Wu Zhao, who usurped the throne of her son, the Emperor Ruizong of Tang, in 690. The dynasty lasted until another one of Wu Zhao's sons, the Emperor Zhongzong of Tang, was restored to the throne in the Shenlong Coup in 705, marking the restoration of the Tang dynasty. Historians generally regard the Wu Zhou as an interregnum of the Tang dynasty.", "type": "ruler", "typeLabel": "Souveraineté", "continents": ["Asie"], "epochs": ["moyen-age"], "from": 691, "to": 704, "itemCount": 120, "items": ["Andong", "Anqing", "Beijing", "Bozhou", "Cao Bang", "Changsha", "Changzhi", "Chaozhou", "Chengde", "Chenzhou", "Dalian", "Daming", "Datong", "Fengyang", "Fengyuan", "Fuyang", "Fuzhou", "Gaizhou", "Gansu", "Ganzhou", "Guangnan", "Guangxi", "Guangzhou", "Guilin", "Guiyang", "Guyuan", "Ha Tinh", "Hainan", "Hami", "Handan", "Hangzhou", "Hanyang", "Hefei", "Hejian", "Hengyang", "Hetu Ala", "Hohhot", "Hongkong", "Hotan", "Huai'an"], "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wu_Zhou", "articleLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "image": "", "imageCredit": {"filename": "Tang_Dynasty_circa_700_CE.png", "artist": "Ian Kiu", "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/", "credit": "This image has been extracted from another file", "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tang_Dynasty_circa_700_CE.png"}, "revision": "", "sha256": "5730311acb6a24f897874eeabcf3f25069194e06eeea486570559ef7eba90e56"}